course: dictionary
lesson: 376
title: Feelings words: anxiety
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anxiety is a noun, a name for a feeling. It means worry, nervousness or fear about what might happen next. Before a test or a big match, you might feel it in your tummy or your heart.
explain: Context gives you clues: «Anxiety is worry or fear, often with a fast heartbeat; everyone has some.» The clues are worry, fear and a fast heartbeat, so anxiety is a feeling that shows in your mind and your body.
explain: Sometimes anxiety is strong and keeps coming back, and then it can make school and sleep hard. Talking to an adult you trust can help, and so can a doctor. Anxiety is not your fault, and you do not have to carry it alone.
explain: People also say «an anxiety» to mean one particular worry, like a worry about a spelling test. Anxiety is the feeling in general; an anxiety is one specific worry.
fact: Anxiety is a noun, and its plural is anxieties.
fact: «Anxiety» means a feeling of worry, nervousness or fear about what might happen.
fact: When anxiety is strong and happens often, it can make life hard, and talking and doctors can help.
fact: Everyday examples are test anxiety and the anxiety you feel before a match.
fact: Ways to calm down include slow breathing and talking to an adult.
exercise: «Anxiety is worry or fear, often with a fast heartbeat; everyone has some.» What is anxiety? | A loud noise in the playground | A type of food eaten at lunch | A feeling of being very tired after sport | *A feeling of worry or fear about what might happen
exercise: Before the spelling test, Kai feels worried and his heart beats fast. Which word names this feeling? | *Anxiety | Joy | Sleepiness | Laughter
exercise: Ella says, «I have an anxiety about the swimming gala.» What does an anxiety mean here? | A whole happy feeling about the day | A kind of sport | A special swimming hat | *One particular worry
test: Which of these is a way the lessons say anxiety can be helped? | Eating lots of sweets | Staying up all night worrying | *Breathing slowly and talking to an adult | Hiding it and never telling anyone
test: What is the plural of anxiety? | *anxieties | anxiouses | anxietys | anxiety's
exam: Which sentence uses «an anxiety» to mean one particular worry? | Anxiety is a fruit that grows on trees | Anxiety is the name of her favourite pet | *Her biggest anxiety was forgetting her lines in the school play | Her anxiety ran across the field
